Paper:arXiv 2611.07457
Authors:Eckhard Platen,Kevin Fergusson
Abstract
Drawing on information-theoretic principles and empirical evidence,a proxy for the growth-optimal portfolio of stocks(the benchmark)is constructed and modeled.The derivative of its activity time captures overreactions in trading behavior and follows a fast-moving,quasi-stationary scalar diffusion.The benchmark’s log-returns are predicted to follow a Student t distribution with degrees of freedom slightly less than four,and this prediction is tested empirically.With the benchmark as numeraire,the derived model enables benchmark-neutral pricing and hedging.
